/-!
# Gauge certificates of the `m ≡ 2 (mod 3)` designs (KN entry, `KN2_net`)

For every design `rows2_p` of `table2`: a gauge `(L, U, μ)` from the constant window `Can 2` to
the design's windows, and inverses `Ti` of the target pivot blocks.  `gcert2_p_ok` checks `CertOK`
(triangularity, nonzero diagonals, the window identity on every needed entry, `Tpad * Ti = 1`, the
zero rows between pivot levels and window) by `decide +kernel` (no `native_decide`).
Generated by `kn_lean/gencert.py` (research repository) from the gauges computed by `solve.py`.
-/

